# punused findings adjudicated as false positives. One literal substring per
# line, matched against punused's output line; full-line `#` comments carry the
# reason.
#
# sse is a LIBRARY (`github.com/cplieger/sse`) that also ships a `main` package
# under ssetest/cmd, the controllable fixture server the TypeScript suites
# drive. The CI gate's app-mode detection ("a main package exists") therefore
# gates it on punused even though its exported surface is a PUBLISHED API.
# punused resolves references through gopls `textDocument/references` inside
# this module only ("It does not detect references from outside of your
# project", its README's first caveat), so every API symbol whose callers live
# in a consumer module is reported EU1002 (no reference) or EU1001 (referenced
# only from this repo's _test.go files). Consumer evidence below was taken
# against the two modules adopting this one (vibekit, subflux); the file and
# call shape are the durable part, line numbers are the snapshot at
# adjudication time.
#
# Hub options a consumer sets when constructing its hub. vibekit
# internal/agent/runtime.go:348-351 passes WithKeepalive, WithKeepaliveEvent,
# WithWriteTimeout and WithReconnectDelay; subflux internal/server/events/bus.go:88
# passes WithMaxClients.
function WithKeepalive
function WithKeepaliveEvent
function WithWriteTimeout
function WithReconnectDelay
function WithMaxClients
#
# Tuning knobs with a documented default that no consumer overrides today. Each
# bounds a resource (ring bytes, digest body bytes, digest subject count) and is
# refused when incoherent with its siblings at New; a consumer whose deployment
# needs a different bound sets it, and until one does the default is the
# contract. README "Constructing a hub" and "The digest" document all three.
function WithReplayMaxBytes
function WithDigestMaxSubjects
function WithDigestMaxBody
#
# Hub methods a consumer calls after construction. SetMaxClients: subflux
# internal/server/server.go:244 re-applies the cap on a config reload.
# Snapshot is the replay ring's diagnostic read (README "Serving and
# publishing"), the counterpart of Position for an operator dumping state.
method (*Hub).SetMaxClients
method (*Hub).Snapshot
#
# The ssetest seam consumers reuse from their own tests (README "Testing
# against the hub"). NewRecorder: vibekit internal/git/handlers_test.go. Serve
# and Frames are the two halves of the same seam and are exercised by this
# module's own tests only until a consumer's suite drives a hub end to end.
function Serve
function NewRecorder
method (*Recorder).Frames
#
# Methods reached through interface assertions rather than direct calls, which
# gopls references cannot see. http.ResponseController discovers
# SetWriteDeadline and SetReadDeadline on the writer it is given and unwraps a
# wrapping writer through Unwrap (serve.go's flush discovery does the same),
# so these three satisfy net/http's contract and are called by it.
method (*Recorder).SetWriteDeadline
method (*Recorder).SetReadDeadline
method (*streamWriter).Unwrap
